# DLe — Description Logic (Extended)
# This document uses standard Description Logic (DL) syntax for ontology axioms, with the following extensions:
#
# Annotations (lines beginning with @):
# @label <IRI> "text"  — display name of the resource
# @doc <IRI> "text"  — description of the resource
# @db <IRI>  — resource appears explicitly in the database using its own identifier
# @db <IRI> "identifier"  — resource appears explicitly in the database and is queried using this identifier
# @storage <IRI> "text"  — describes database storage details
# @ann <IRI> <annotation-property> "text"  — annotation using the given property
# @prefix <prefix>: <namespace>  — declares a prefix
# @import <IRI>  — imports another ontology
# @ontology <IRI>  — declares the ontology IRI
#
# Naming conventions:
# - Every entity has an implicit label equal to its identifier unless @label is declared
# - Unprefixed names (e.g., Application) are in the default namespace (:Application)
# - Prefixed names use declared prefixes (e.g., xsd:string)
# - Concept/class identifiers conventionally begin with an upper-case letter
# - Role/reference/field identifiers conventionally begin with a lower-case letter
#
# Database convention:
# - Resources only appear explicitly in the database if they have an @db annotation
#
# DLe extensions:
# ≝  — defines a symbol or predicate; right-hand side is not DL and is not required to be valid OWL
# ∃r₁,…,rₙ.P  — predicate restriction: P(r₁,…,rₙ) holds over the role values

@import "metaschema.dle"

ApplicationsWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
OrganizationWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
PeopleWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
@label ApplicationsWorkspace "Applications Workspace"
@label BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace "Business Capabilities Workspace"
@label OrganizationWorkspace "Organization Workspace"
@label PeopleWorkspace "People Workspace"
@doc ApplicationsWorkspace "Workspace for application portfolio modeling."
@doc BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace "Workspace for business capability modeling (capability maps / hierarchies)."
@doc OrganizationWorkspace "Workspace for modeling organizational structure (organizations and organizational units)."
@doc PeopleWorkspace "Workspace for modeling people and their roles/responsibilities (supports surveys/notifications)."

Application ⊑ Component
Application ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.ApplicationsWorkspace
@db Application

BusinessCapability ⊑ Component
BusinessCapability ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace
@label BusinessCapability "Business Capability"
@doc BusinessCapability "Represents what an organization does; typically modeled as a hierarchical capability map."
@db BusinessCapability

Organization ⊑ Component
Organization ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.OrganizationWorkspace

@doc Organization "Represents an organization or enterprise; may contain organizational units or sub-organizations."
@db Organization

OrganizationalUnit ⊑ Component
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.OrganizationWorkspace
@label OrganizationalUnit "Organizational Unit"
@doc OrganizationalUnit "Subdivision of an organization (e.g., department/team); may be related via hierarchy or belongsTo links."
@db OrganizationalUnit

Person ⊑ Component
Person ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.PeopleWorkspace
@doc Person "Named individual represented in the model, typically linked to other components via roles or responsibilities."
@db Person

BelongingEntity ⊑ Component
BelongingContainer ⊑ Component
@label BelongingEntity "Belonging Entity"
@label BelongingContainer "Belonging Container"
@doc BelongingEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of a belongsTo reference. Foundation identifies Person and OrganizationalUnit as known belonging entities; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc BelongingContainer "An entity eligible to be the target of a belongsTo reference. Foundation identifies Organization and OrganizationalUnit as known belonging containers; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Person ⊑ BelongingEntity
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ BelongingEntity
Organization ⊑ BelongingContainer
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ BelongingContainer

belongsTo ⊑ reference
∃belongsTo.⊤ ⊑ BelongingEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀belongsTo.BelongingContainer
@db belongsTo "Belongs To"
@label belongsTo "Belongs To"
@doc belongsTo "Relates a BelongingEntity to a BelongingContainer. In Foundation, a Person belongs to an OrganizationalUnit, while an OrganizationalUnit may belong to an Organization or another OrganizationalUnit. OrganizationalUnit relationships are used for non-hierarchical organizational structures; hierarchical structures use parent."

Person ⊑ ∀belongsTo.OrganizationalUnit
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∀belongsTo.(Organization ⊔ OrganizationalUnit)

ConsumingEntity ⊑ Component
ConsumableEntity ⊑ Component
@label ConsumingEntity "Consuming Entity"
@label ConsumableEntity "Consumable Entity"
@doc ConsumingEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of a consumes reference. Foundation identifies OrganizationalUnit as a known consuming entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc ConsumableEntity "An entity eligible to be the target of a consumes reference. Foundation identifies Application as a known consumable entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ConsumingEntity
Application ⊑ ConsumableEntity

consumes ⊑ reference
∃consumes.⊤ ⊑ ConsumingEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀consumes.ConsumableEntity
@db consumes "Consumes"
@label consumes "Consumes"
@doc consumes "Relates a ConsumingEntity to a ConsumableEntity that it consumes, may consume, or gains value from."

LifecycleRelatedEntity ⊑ Component
@label LifecycleRelatedEntity "Lifecycle Related Entity"
@doc LifecycleRelatedEntity "An entity eligible to participate as either endpoint of a hasLifecycleRelation reference. Foundation identifies Application as a known lifecycle-related entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Application ⊑ LifecycleRelatedEntity

hasLifecycleRelation ⊑ reference
∃hasLifecycleRelation.⊤ ⊑ LifecycleRelatedEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀hasLifecycleRelation.LifecycleRelatedEntity
@db hasLifecycleRelation "Has Successor"
@label hasLifecycleRelation "Has Successor"
@doc hasLifecycleRelation "Time-based dependency, succession, or replacement between lifecycle-related entities. The role name better reflects the relation than the stored label."

hasTimedDependency ⊑ hasLifecycleRelation
isSucceededBy ⊑ hasLifecycleRelation
replacedBy ⊑ hasLifecycleRelation
hasTimedDependency ⊓ isSucceededBy ⊑ ⊥
hasTimedDependency ⊓ replacedBy ⊑ ⊥
isSucceededBy ⊓ replacedBy ⊑ ⊥
@doc hasTimedDependency "Time-based dependency. This is one of the uses of hasLifecycleRelation"
@doc isSucceededBy "Describes the application to use after this one. This is one of the uses of hasLifecycleRelation"
@doc replacedBy "Replacement for an application. This is one of the uses of hasLifecycleRelation"

ExpertEntity ⊑ Component
ExpertiseSubject ⊑ Component
@label ExpertEntity "Expert Entity"
@label ExpertiseSubject "Expertise Subject"
@doc ExpertEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of an isExpertIn reference. Foundation identifies Person as a known expert entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc ExpertiseSubject "An entity eligible to be the target of an isExpertIn reference. Foundation identifies Application and BusinessCapability as known expertise subjects; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Person ⊑ ExpertEntity
Application ⊑ ExpertiseSubject
BusinessCapability ⊑ ExpertiseSubject

isExpertIn ⊑ reference
∃isExpertIn.⊤ ⊑ ExpertEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀isExpertIn.ExpertiseSubject
@db isExpertIn "Is Expert In"
@label isExpertIn "Is Expert In"
@doc isExpertIn "Relates an ExpertEntity to an ExpertiseSubject about which it has expert knowledge; often used to identify survey recipients."

RealizableEntity ⊑ Component
RealizingEntity ⊑ Component
@label RealizableEntity "Realizable Entity"
@label RealizingEntity "Realizing Entity"
@doc RealizableEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of an isRealizedBy reference. Foundation identifies BusinessCapability as a known realizable entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc RealizingEntity "An entity eligible to be the target of an isRealizedBy reference. Foundation identifies Application and OrganizationalUnit as known realizing entities; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

BusinessCapability ⊑ RealizableEntity
Application ⊑ RealizingEntity
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ RealizingEntity

isRealizedBy ⊑ reference
∃isRealizedBy.⊤ ⊑ RealizableEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀isRealizedBy.RealizingEntity
@db isRealizedBy "Is Realized By"
@label isRealizedBy "Is Realized By"
@doc isRealizedBy "Relates a RealizableEntity to a RealizingEntity that directly implements it, in whole or in part."

descendant ∘ isRealizedBy ⊑ isRealizedByDescendent
@doc isRealizedByDescendent "Relates an entity to a RealizingEntity that directly implements one of its descendants, in whole or in part."

OwningEntity ⊑ Component
Ownable ⊑ Component
@label OwningEntity "Owning Entity"
@doc OwningEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of an owns reference. Foundation identifies Person as a known owning entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc Ownable "An entity eligible to be the target of an owns reference. Foundation identifies Application and OrganizationalUnit as known ownable entities; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Person ⊑ OwningEntity
Application ⊑ Ownable
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ Ownable

owns ⊑ reference
∃owns.⊤ ⊑ OwningEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀owns.Ownable
@db owns "Owns"
@label owns "Owns"
@doc owns "Relates an OwningEntity to an Ownable for which it has overall responsibility."

Organization ⊑ ∀parent.Organization
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∃parent.⊤
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∀parent.(Organization ⊔ OrganizationalUnit)
BusinessCapability ⊑ ∀parent.BusinessCapability

ReportingEntity ⊑ Component
ReportRecipient ⊑ Component
@label ReportingEntity "Reporting Entity"
@label ReportRecipient "Report Recipient"
@doc ReportingEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of a reportsTo reference. Foundation identifies Person as a known reporting entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc ReportRecipient "An entity eligible to be the target of a reportsTo reference. Foundation identifies Person as a known report recipient; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Person ⊑ ReportingEntity
Person ⊑ ReportRecipient

reportsTo ⊑ reference
∃reportsTo.⊤ ⊑ ReportingEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀reportsTo.ReportRecipient
@db reportsTo "Reports To"
@label reportsTo "Reports To"
@doc reportsTo "Relates a ReportingEntity to the ReportRecipient to which it is accountable or reports."

applicationOwnershipState ⊑ calculatedList
∃applicationOwnershipState.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀applicationOwnershipState.{"Managed","Nominated","Owned","Unowned"}
≤1 applicationOwnershipState.⊤
@db applicationOwnershipState "application_ownership_state"
@label applicationOwnershipState "Application Ownership State"
@doc applicationOwnershipState "Calculated Ownership lifecycle state: Unowned (no owner), Nominated (pending acceptance), Owned (owner assigned but stale or incomplete data), Managed (current owner with up-to-date strategic data). Calculated hourly using owner presence, ownershipAccepted, strategicRating, and reviewDate freshness (≈7 months)."

Unowned ≡ Application ⊓ ¬∃owns⁻.⊤
Unowned ≡ ∃applicationOwnershipState.{"Unowned"}
Nominated ≡ Application ⊓ ∃owns⁻.⊤ ⊓ ∃ownershipAccepted.{"No"}
Nominated ≡ ∃applicationOwnershipState.{"Nominated"}
Owned ≡ Application ⊓ ∃owns⁻.⊤ ⊓ ∃ownershipAccepted.{"Yes"} ⊓ ¬∃strategicRating.⊤
Owned ≡ ∃applicationOwnershipState.{"Owned"}
Managed ≡ Application ⊓ ∃owns⁻.⊤ ⊓ ∃ownershipAccepted.{"Yes"} ⊓ ∃strategicRating.⊤
Managed ≡ ∃applicationOwnershipState.{"Managed"}

propertyTIME ⊑ field
⊤ ⊑ ∀propertyTIME.(xsd:integer ⊔ xsd:decimal ⊔ xsd:string)
@label propertyTIME "TIME Rating and Dimension Fields"
@doc propertyTIME "A group of fields encapsulating the Gartner TIME model dimensions (business value, technical fit) used for application portfolio assessment."

applicationType ⊑ field
∃applicationType.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀applicationType.{"COTS","Internally Developed","3rd Party Custom Developed"}
≤1 applicationType.⊤
@db applicationType "application_type"
@label applicationType "Application Type"
@doc applicationType "Delivery model: Commerical Off The Shelf (COTS), Internally Developed, or 3rd Party Custom Developed."

approved ⊑ field
∃approved.⊤ ⊑ Application ⊔ BusinessCapability
⊤ ⊑ ∀approved.xsd:boolean
≤1 approved.⊤
@db approved
@label approved "Approved"
@doc approved "Review/acknowledgement flag for a component’s accuracy/completeness."

businessStrategicFit ⊑ field
∃businessStrategicFit.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀businessStrategicFit.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 businessStrategicFit.⊤
@db businessStrategicFit "business_strategic_fit"
@label businessStrategicFit "Business Strategic Fit"
@doc businessStrategicFit "Score for how well an application supports business strategy / user ambitions."

functionalFit ⊑ field
∃functionalFit.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀functionalFit.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 functionalFit.⊤
@db functionalFit "functional_fit"
@label functionalFit "Functional Fit"
@doc functionalFit "Functional fit score (meets required functionality), 1..5."

featuresAndUsability ⊑ propertyTIME
∃featuresAndUsability.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀featuresAndUsability.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 featuresAndUsability.⊤
@db featuresAndUsability "features_and_usability"
@label featuresAndUsability "Features and Usability"
@doc featuresAndUsability "Usability score (ease of use / training burden), 1..5."

criticality ⊑ propertyTIME
∃criticality.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀criticality.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 criticality.⊤
@db criticality
@label criticality "Criticality"
@doc criticality "Ordinal business impact score 1..5 (5 = high impact, 1 = negligible)."

∃businessStrategicFitValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀businessStrategicFitValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 businessStrategicFitValue.⊤
@doc businessStrategicFitValue "Numeric equivalent to the businessStrategicFit property"
∃businessStrategicFitValue.{1} ≡ ∃businessStrategicFit.{"1"}
∃businessStrategicFitValue.{2} ≡ ∃businessStrategicFit.{"2"}
∃businessStrategicFitValue.{3} ≡ ∃businessStrategicFit.{"3"}
∃businessStrategicFitValue.{4} ≡ ∃businessStrategicFit.{"4"}
∃businessStrategicFitValue.{5} ≡ ∃businessStrategicFit.{"5"}

∃functionalFitValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀functionalFitValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 functionalFitValue.⊤
@doc functionalFitValue "Numeric equivalent to the functionalFit property"
∃functionalFitValue.{1} ≡ ∃functionalFit.{"1"}
∃functionalFitValue.{2} ≡ ∃functionalFit.{"2"}
∃functionalFitValue.{3} ≡ ∃functionalFit.{"3"}
∃functionalFitValue.{4} ≡ ∃functionalFit.{"4"}
∃functionalFitValue.{5} ≡ ∃functionalFit.{"5"}

∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀featuresAndUsabilityValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 featuresAndUsabilityValue.⊤
@doc featuresAndUsabilityValue "Numeric equivalent to the featuresAndUsability property"
∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.{1} ≡ ∃featuresAndUsability.{"1"}
∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.{2} ≡ ∃featuresAndUsability.{"2"}
∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.{3} ≡ ∃featuresAndUsability.{"3"}
∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.{4} ≡ ∃featuresAndUsability.{"4"}
∃featuresAndUsabilityValue.{5} ≡ ∃featuresAndUsability.{"5"}

∃criticalityValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀criticalityValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 criticalityValue.⊤
@doc criticalityValue "Numeric equivalent to the criticality property"
∃criticalityValue.{1} ≡ ∃criticality.{"1"}
∃criticalityValue.{2} ≡ ∃criticality.{"2"}
∃criticalityValue.{3} ≡ ∃criticality.{"3"}
∃criticalityValue.{4} ≡ ∃criticality.{"4"}
∃criticalityValue.{5} ≡ ∃criticality.{"5"}

businessValue ⊑ propertyTIME
businessValue ⊑ calculatedNumber
∃businessValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀businessValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 businessValue.⊤
@db businessValue "business_value"
@label businessValue "Business Value"
@doc businessValue "Calculated score assessing how well an application supports current and future user needs: businessValue = (businessStrategicFitValue * 0.25) + (functionalFitValue * 0.2) + (featuresAndUsabilityValue * 0.2) + (criticalityValue * 0.35)"

complexity ⊑ calculatedNumber
⊤ ⊑ ∀complexity.xsd:integer
∃complexity.⊤ ⊑ BusinessCapability
≤1 complexity.⊤
@db complexity
@label complexity "Complexity"
@doc complexity "Calculated complexity of a business capability: total number of isRealizedBy references from the capability and all descendant capabilities to Applications or Organizational Units."

componentLevel ⊑ calculatedNumber
∃componentLevel.⊤ ⊑ BusinessCapability
≤1 componentLevel.⊤
@db componentLevel "component_level"
@label componentLevel "Component Level"
@doc componentLevel "Calculated depth/level in the capability hierarchy (useful for filtering)."

contactEmail ⊑ field
∃contactEmail.⊤ ⊑ Person
⊤ ⊑ ∀contactEmail.xsd:string
≤1 contactEmail.⊤
@db contactEmail "contact_email"
@label contactEmail "Contact Email"
@doc contactEmail "Email-like identifier (contains '@'); validate externally if needed."

liveStartDate ⊑ field
∃liveStartDate.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀liveStartDate.xsd:dateTime
≤1 liveStartDate.⊤
@db liveStartDate "live_start_date"
@label liveStartDate "Live Start Date"
@doc liveStartDate "Go-live date."

liveEndDate ⊑ field
∃liveEndDate.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀liveEndDate.xsd:dateTime
≤1 liveEndDate.⊤
@db liveEndDate "live_end_date"
@label liveEndDate "Live End Date"
@doc liveEndDate "Proposed end-of-life."

hostingType ⊑ field
∃hostingType.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀hostingType.{"3rd. Party","Cloud","Desktop","Hybrid","On Premise","SaaS"}
≤1 hostingType.⊤
@db hostingType "hosting_type"
@label hostingType "Hosting Type"

lifecyclePhase ⊑ field
∃lifecyclePhase.⊤ ⊑ Application ⊔ BusinessCapability
⊤ ⊑ ∀lifecyclePhase.{"Implementing","Live","Phasing Out","Retired"}
≤1 lifecyclePhase.⊤
@db lifecyclePhase "lifecycle_phase"
@label lifecyclePhase "Lifecycle Phase"

marketDifferentiation ⊑ field
∃marketDifferentiation.⊤ ⊑ BusinessCapability
⊤ ⊑ ∀marketDifferentiation.xsd:decimal[≥1 ⊓ ≤5]
≤1 marketDifferentiation.⊤
@db marketDifferentiation "market_differentiation"
@label marketDifferentiation "Market Differentiation"
@doc marketDifferentiation "Ordinal score (1..5) of competitive advantage provided by a business capability: from commodity (1) to market-disruptive (5)."

maturity ⊑ field
∃maturity.⊤ ⊑ BusinessCapability
⊤ ⊑ ∀maturity.xsd:integer[≥1 ⊓ ≤5]
≤1 maturity.⊤
@db maturity
@label maturity "Maturity"
@doc maturity "Ordinal maturity score (1..5): Initial, Under Development, Defined, Managed, Measured."

ownershipAccepted ⊑ field
∃ownershipAccepted.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀ownershipAccepted.{"No","Yes"}
≤1 ownershipAccepted.⊤
@db ownershipAccepted "ownership_accepted"
@label ownershipAccepted "Ownership Accepted"
@doc ownershipAccepted "Whether a nominated owner has accepted responsibility."

reviewDate ⊑ field
∃reviewDate.⊤ ⊑ Application ⊔ BusinessCapability
⊤ ⊑ ∀reviewDate.xsd:dateTime
≤1 reviewDate.⊤
@db reviewDate "review_date"
@label reviewDate "Review Date"
@doc reviewDate "Date a component was reviewed/acknowledged as accurate and complete."

serviceLevel ⊑ field
∃serviceLevel.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀serviceLevel.{"Bronze","Silver","Gold","Platinum"}
≤1 serviceLevel.⊤
@db serviceLevel "service_level"
@label serviceLevel "Service Level"
@doc serviceLevel "Application importance / fix-on-fail priority (Bronze..Platinum)."

technicalIntegrity ⊑ propertyTIME
∃technicalIntegrity.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀technicalIntegrity.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 technicalIntegrity.⊤
@db technicalIntegrity "technical_integrity"
@label technicalIntegrity "Technical Integrity"
@doc technicalIntegrity "Adherence to technical standards, 1..5."

technicalStrategicFit ⊑ propertyTIME
∃technicalStrategicFit.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀technicalStrategicFit.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 technicalStrategicFit.⊤
@db technicalStrategicFit "technical_strategic_fit"
@label technicalStrategicFit "Technical Strategic Fit"
@doc technicalStrategicFit "Future-proofing / technical strategic alignment score, 1..5."

maintainabilityAndAgility ⊑ propertyTIME
∃maintainabilityAndAgility.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀maintainabilityAndAgility.{"1", "2", "3", "4", "5"}
≤1 maintainabilityAndAgility.⊤
@db maintainabilityAndAgility "maintainability_and_agility"
@label maintainabilityAndAgility "Maintainability and Agility"
@doc maintainabilityAndAgility "Score for ease of maintenance and adaptability within the technology landscape, 1..5."

∃technicalIntegrityValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀technicalIntegrityValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 technicalIntegrityValue.⊤
@doc technicalIntegrityValue "Numeric equivalent to the technicalIntegrity property"
∃technicalIntegrityValue.{1} ≡ ∃technicalIntegrity.{"1"}
∃technicalIntegrityValue.{2} ≡ ∃technicalIntegrity.{"2"}
∃technicalIntegrityValue.{3} ≡ ∃technicalIntegrity.{"3"}
∃technicalIntegrityValue.{4} ≡ ∃technicalIntegrity.{"4"}
∃technicalIntegrityValue.{5} ≡ ∃technicalIntegrity.{"5"}

∃technicalStrategicFitValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀technicalStrategicFitValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 technicalStrategicFitValue.⊤
@doc technicalStrategicFitValue "Numeric equivalent to the technicalStrategicFit property"
∃technicalStrategicFitValue.{1} ≡ ∃technicalStrategicFit.{"1"}
∃technicalStrategicFitValue.{2} ≡ ∃technicalStrategicFit.{"2"}
∃technicalStrategicFitValue.{3} ≡ ∃technicalStrategicFit.{"3"}
∃technicalStrategicFitValue.{4} ≡ ∃technicalStrategicFit.{"4"}
∃technicalStrategicFitValue.{5} ≡ ∃technicalStrategicFit.{"5"}

∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.xsd:decimal
≤1 maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.⊤
@doc maintainabilityAndAgilityValue "Numeric equivalent to the maintainabilityAndAgility property"
∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.{1} ≡ ∃maintainabilityAndAgility.{"1"}
∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.{2} ≡ ∃maintainabilityAndAgility.{"2"}
∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.{3} ≡ ∃maintainabilityAndAgility.{"3"}
∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.{4} ≡ ∃maintainabilityAndAgility.{"4"}
∃maintainabilityAndAgilityValue.{5} ≡ ∃maintainabilityAndAgility.{"5"}

technicalFit ⊑ propertyTIME
technicalFit ⊑ calculatedNumber
∃technicalFit.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀technicalFit.xsd:decimal
≤1 technicalFit.⊤
@db technicalFit "technical_fit"
@label technicalFit "Technical Fit"
@doc technicalFit "Weighted aggregate (rounded to 2 decimals): techicalFit = (technicalIntegrityValue * 0.43) + (maintainabilityAndAgilityValue * 0.27) + (technicalStrategicFitValue * 0.3)"

strategicRating ⊑ propertyTIME
strategicRating ⊑ calculatedList
∃strategicRating.⊤ ⊑ Application
⊤ ⊑ ∀strategicRating.{"Eliminate","Invest","Migrate","Tolerate"}
≤1 strategicRating.⊤
@db strategicRating "strategic_rating"
@label strategicRating "Strategic Rating"
@doc strategicRating "Calculated Gartner TIME strategic quadrant category. Note that this value is not a decision and may not be approved"

∃strategicRating.{"Eliminate"} ≡ ∃technicalFit.xsd:decimal[<3] ⊓ ∃businessValue.xsd:decimal[<3]
∃strategicRating.{"Invest"} ≡ ∃technicalFit.xsd:decimal[≥3] ⊓ ∃businessValue.xsd:decimal[≥3]
∃strategicRating.{"Migrate"} ≡ ∃technicalFit.xsd:decimal[<3] ⊓ ∃businessValue.xsd:decimal[≥3]
∃strategicRating.{"Tolerate"} ≡ ∃technicalFit.xsd:decimal[≥3] ⊓ ∃businessValue.xsd:decimal[<3]

# The following extends the model with definitions not saved in the database

# Inverses named for convenience
consumedBy ≡ consumes⁻
realizes ≡ isRealizedBy⁻
ownedBy ≡ owns⁻
hasExpert ≡ isExpertIn⁻

parent ∘ parent⁻ ⊑ sibling
# irreflexivity for a composed property is outside of OWL, but siblings must be irreflexive
Irref(sibling)


HighCriticality ≡ ∃criticality.{"4", "5"}
LowCriticality ≡ ∃criticality.{"1", "2"}
HighServiceLevel ≡ ∃serviceLevel.{"Gold","Platinum"}
LowServiceLevel ≡ ∃serviceLevel.{"Bronze","Silver"}
KeyApplication ≡ Application ⨅ (HighCriticality ⨆ HighServiceLevel)

Implementing ≡ ∃lifecyclePhase.{"Implementing"}
LivePhase ≡ ∃lifecyclePhase.{"Live"}
PhasingOut ≡ ∃lifecyclePhase.{"Phasing Out"}
Retired ≡ ∃lifecyclePhase.{"Retired"}

HasLiveStart ≡ ∃liveStartDate.⊤
HasLiveEnd ≡ ∃liveEndDate.⊤
HasLive ≡ (HasLiveStart ⊔ HasLiveEnd)

# The following expressions extend DL using predicates, and extend OWL using DL predicate restrictions
greaterThan(x,y) ≝ x > y
afterNow(x) ≝ x > now()
beforeNow(x) ≝ x < now()
onOrBeforeNow(x) ≝ x ≤ now()
enclosesNow(x,y) ≝ x ≤ now() ∧ now() ≤ y
withinNextYear(x) ≝ now() < x ∧ x < addDuration(now(), P1Y)

LiveStartAfterEnd ≡ ∃liveStartDate,liveEndDate.greaterThan
LiveStartsInFuture ≡ ∃liveStartDate.afterNow
LiveEndedInPast ≡ ∃liveEndDate.beforeNow
LiveNow ≡ ∃liveStartDate,liveEndDate.enclosesNow
LiveNowOpenEnded ≡ ∃liveStartDate.onOrBeforeNow ⊓ ¬∃liveEndDate.⊤
